---
import ConsiliumCaseLayout from '../../../layouts/ConsiliumCaseLayout.astro';
---
<ConsiliumCaseLayout title="Consilium Medicum Google Ads case" description="3,356 tracked Google Ads conversions for Consilium Medicum at €3.25 average cost per conversion." eyebrow="GOOGLE ADS" headline="3,356 enquiries" accent="at €3.25." intro="A performance case built around existing patient demand: capture the search, match it with the right medical service and measure the response — not just the click." metrics={[{value:'3,356',label:'tracked conversions · 2024'},{value:'€3.25',label:'average cost / conversion'},{value:'€0.20',label:'average CPC'},{value:'4.17–7.42%',label:'lead conversion range'}]}>
<section class="case-section shell"><div class="two"><span class="eyebrow">THE JOB</span><div><h2>Patients were already searching.</h2><p class="statement">The opportunity was not to create demand. It was to intercept high-intent demand at the moment a patient was looking for care.</p><p>For a medical clinic, that means many different services, symptoms and specialists — each with different search intent. We treated Google Ads as a patient-acquisition system rather than one generic campaign.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="visual"><div class="shell"><span class="eyebrow">PATIENT JOURNEY</span><div class="path"><div><b>01</b><h3>Need</h3><p>A patient has a symptom, diagnosis or need for a specialist.</p></div><i>→</i><div><b>02</b><h3>Search</h3><p>They actively search Google for the relevant medical service.</p></div><i>→</i><div><b>03</b><h3>Match</h3><p>The ad and landing page answer that specific intent.</p></div><i>→</i><div><b>04</b><h3>Enquiry</h3><p>The patient calls or submits a lead action.</p></div></div><div class="dashboard"><div><span>GOOGLE ADS / 2024</span><span>CONSILIUM MEDICUM</span></div><strong>3,356</strong><p>TRACKED CONVERSIONS</p><div class="dashgrid"><span><b>€3.25</b> CPA</span><span><b>€0.20</b> CPC</span><span><b>4.17–7.42%</b> LEAD CR</span></div></div></div></section>
<section class="case-section dark"><div class="shell two"><span class="eyebrow">HOW WE RAN IT</span><div><h2>Structure around intent,<br/>not around traffic.</h2><div class="data-list"><div class="data-row"><span>Search intent</span><span>Separate medical needs instead of sending every query into the same message.</span><strong>01</strong></div><div class="data-row"><span>Relevant pages</span><span>Match the patient’s query with a page that explains the service and next action.</span><strong>02</strong></div><div class="data-row"><span>Conversion tracking</span><span>Optimise around calls and lead actions rather than clicks alone.</span><strong>03</strong></div><div class="data-row"><span>Ongoing optimisation</span><span>Budgets and campaigns changed with demand, capacity and performance.</span><strong>04</strong></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="case-section shell"><div class="two"><span class="eyebrow">MEASUREMENT NOTE</span><div><h2>We only claim<br/>what was measured.</h2><p class="statement">The historical reporting tracked calls and lead actions as Google Ads conversions.</p><p>CRM-to-visit attribution was not fully integrated at that time, so this case does not turn 3,356 conversions into an invented number of appointments, patients or revenue.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="accent-section"><div class="shell"><span class="eyebrow">RESULT</span><h2>3,356 measurable patient actions.<br/>€3.25 average cost.</h2><div class="flow"><span>NEED</span><b>→</b><span>SEARCH</span><b>→</b><span>AD</span><b>→</b><span>SERVICE PAGE</span><b>→</b><span>CALL / LEAD</span></div></div></section>
</ConsiliumCaseLayout>
